problem:
Squares $ABCD$ and $EFGH$ are equal in area.  Vertices $B$, $E$, $C$, and $H$ lie on the same line.  Diagonal $AC$ is extended to $J$, the midpoint of $GH$.  What is the fraction of the two squares that is shaded? [asy]
fill((0,4)--(4,4)--(4,0)--cycle,gray);
fill((4,0)--(6,0)--(6,-2)--cycle,gray);
draw((0,0)--(4,0)--(4,4)--(0,4)--cycle,linewidth(1));
draw((2,0)--(6,0)--(6,-4)--(2,-4)--cycle,linewidth(1));
draw((0,4)--(6,-2),linewidth(1));
label("$A$",(0,4),NW);
label("$B$",(0,0),W);
label("$C$",(4,0),NE);
label("$D$",(4,4),NE);
label("$E$",(2,0),SW);
label("$F$",(2,-4),SW);
label("$G$",(6,-4),SE);
label("$H$",(6,0),E);
label("$J$",(6,-2),E);
[/asy]The answer is in the form  rac{m}{n}, where gcd(m, n) = 1. Please provide the value of m + n.

How many paths are there from $A$ to $B$ on the lines of the grid shown, if every step must be up or to the right?[asy]size(3cm,3cm);int w=6;int h=3;int i;for (i=0; i<h; ++i){ draw((0,i) -- (w-1,i));}for (i=0; i<w; ++i){ draw((i, 0)--(i,h-1));}label("$B$", (w-1,h-1), NE);label("$A$", (0,0), SW);[/asy]
For example, here is one such valid path highlighted in blue:
[asy]
size(3cm,3cm);
int w=6;
int h=3;
int i;
for (i=0; i<h; ++i){ 
draw((0,i) -- (w-1,i));
}for (i=0; i<w; ++i){ 
draw((i, 0)--(i,h-1));
}
label("$B$", (w-1,h-1), NE);
label("$A$", (0,0), SW);

draw((0,0)--(1,0), blue+1.5);
draw((1,0)--(1,1), blue+1.5);
draw((1,1)--(2,1), blue+1.5);
draw((2,1)--(3,1), blue+1.5);
draw((3,1)--(4,1), blue+1.5);
draw((4,1)--(4,2), blue+1.5);
draw((4,2)--(5,2), blue+1.5);
[/asy]

